  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q4",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Consider the function\n\n$$f(x)=\\frac{x+x^{-1}}{x-x^{-1}}.$$",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $f(x)=\\frac{x^2+1}{x^2-1}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Multiplying the numerator and denominator by $x$ gives $f(x)=\\frac{x^2+1}{x^2-1}$ on the original domain $x\\ne0,\\pm1$.",
          "worked": "The original expression requires $x\\ne0$ and $x-x^{-1}\\ne0$, so $x\\ne0,\\pm1$. Multiply the numerator and denominator by $x$. $$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\frac{x(x+x^{-1})}{x(x-x^{-1})}\\\\ f(x)&=\\frac{x^2+1}{x^2-1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find $f'(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\frac{4x}{(x^2-1)^2}$, for $x\\ne0,\\pm1$.",
          "worked": "Apply the quotient rule to the form from part (a). $$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\frac{2x(x^2-1)-2x(x^2+1)}{(x^2-1)^2}\\\\ f'(x)&=\\frac{2x^3-2x-2x^3-2x}{(x^2-1)^2}\\\\ f'(x)&=-\\frac{4x}{(x^2-1)^2}\\end{align*}$$ The derivative applies on the original domain $x\\ne0,\\pm1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
